The primary focus of this study is to evaluate the effectiveness of various prompting techniques, i.e., Zero-Shot, Few-Shot, and Chain-of-Thought (CoT) in both closed and open-source LLMs for low-resource languages like Bengali. This evaluation is carried out across four downstream tasks using a Bengali dataset denoted as
